Resound consists of several projects which are compiled separately;
instead of making a complex single makefile, we've set up some
simple scripts to do compilation for you.  We'll put these into
a main makefile later when Rhapsody's makefile facility calms down.

./Clean			Cleans out all object files, modules, and
			Resound.app from the Source directory. Puts the
			Source directory into a pristine state.

./Build			Builds Resound.app and the modules for your
	  		architecture.  Resound.app shows up in the 
			Source directory.  The modules show up in the
			Source/ModuleBinaries directory.

./BuildFat		Same as ./Build, except it builds for both PPC
			and Intel target architectures.

./BuildModules		Builds just the modules for your architecture.
			They show up in the Source/ModuleBinaries 
			directory.

./BuildFatModules	Same as ./BuildModules, except it builds for
			both PPC and Intel target architectures.

./OpenAllProjects	Opens all project files (of both Resound and
			Modules) in ProjectBuilder.

./FinallyInstall	Takes one argument, which is the directory to
			install the distribution in.  In this directory,
			./FinallyInstall will create the following
			files or directories: (1) API, the API headers,
			(2) ResoundModules, which holds stripped versions
			of the modules built into Source/ModuleBinaries,
			(3) README.html, copied from the Source directory,
			(4) Resound.app, copied from the Source directory
			and properly stripped.  To complete the
			distribution, you should clean the Source
			directory, then copy it or move it into the
			distribution installation directory.

EXAMPLE:
If you've just unpacked the Resound distribution, and you'd like to
completely reinstall the distribution, do the following:

	cd Source
	./BuildFat
	./FinallyInstall ..
	./Clean

Since Source is already in the distribution directory, you don't need to
move it.

